Phase-3 allocation/wage settlement, household consumption, persistent employer stock, Phase-13 demography/migration, M6 institutions and M5+ remain separate requirements."
REQ-PRODUCTION-003,PARTIAL,578,579,,"PR #579 implements the Phase-3 regional labor-allocation slice of Handoff/05 section 13 over the already-implemented LaborSupplyPlan and LaborDemandPlan: region×labor-category grouping, supply-weighted opening/prior-close cohort wageSignal as regional reference wage with canonical starting-wage fallback, bounded wage-attractiveness weighting, capped proportional employer water-filling with stable unitId residual correction, proportional cohort allocation, and stable cohortId→unitId two-pointer matching into tick-scoped LaborAllocation records. Focused regressions in src/simulation/laborAllocation.test.ts prove matched-total conservation, cohort-supply and unit-demand caps, bounded higher-wage advantage, supply-weighted wage evidence, insertion-order invariance and stable IDs, region/category isolation, zero/tiny quantity handling, malformed/non-finite/duplicate-plan fail-fast behavior, floating residual correction and no WorldState mutation. Code head 06f3fa2bd6b096d6e8254ff680622391b48c33f3 passed TypeScript typecheck/tests/build and policy guard after handoff metadata correction; retained .NET build/test also passed on the same code revision. REQ-PRODUCTION-003 remains PARTIAL: Phase-15 sticky next-tick wage-offer updates are still outstanding and Phase-5 wage settlement belongs to REQ-PRODUCTION-004; no persistent employer stock or M5+ behavior is claimed."
